      "label": "Order event schema",
      "href": "https://example.com/acme/schemas/order-placed"
     }
    ],
    "tldr": "An order is written once, in one Postgres transaction, together with an `order.placed` row in the outbox. The outbox relay publishes that row to the `order-events` topic, and the fulfilment worker turns it into a pick ticket in the warehouse system. If a ticket is missing, the order row exists but the event never left the outbox: check the relay first."
   },
